{
  "description": "The SCR-06 vault matcher (D-38): SPEC SCR-06 step 3 as fixed by R-15, ARCH §8.4, AC-042, AC-110, AC-088. Single source of truth for web/src/tier0/fuzzy.test.ts and web/src/ai/vaultScan.test.ts (Vitest) and the iOS XCTest port (SPEC §10.7, AC-168). Each case has an `fn` naming the function under test, a human `name`, its inputs and `expect`.",
  "conventions": [
    "threshold is RC fuzzy_threshold (0.8, clamped 0.6-0.98) unless a case gives its own `threshold`.",
    "fn match: `term` names an entry of `terms` (digit = kind is plate, house_number or phone). `mode` image = OCR words: `words` (one OCR line) or `lines` (a list of OCR lines, each a list of words). `mode` text = a prompt or echo string in `text`, split on whitespace into words. expect.match is whether the term occurs; expect.spans, when given, is the merged list of [first, last] word indices to mask, counted over all words in order.",
    "Text kinds: normalise (NFKD, no diacritics, lowercase, apostrophes deleted, & -> and, other punctuation -> space), join runs of >= 2 single-character tokens on one OCR line, fold saint/street -> st, avenue -> ave, road -> rd, number -> no, then compare token skeletons (0->o, 1/l->i, 5->s, 8->b, only in tokens with a letter): similarity = 1 - levenshtein / maxLength >= threshold, and tokens of <= 3 characters must be equal. Multi-word labels: one distinctive token (>= 4 chars, not generic), or two consecutive label tokens (not two function words) against two consecutive tokens, or the whole label.",
    "Digit kinds: letters and digits only, uppercase, no confusables; equal to one word or to adjacent words joined (up to 2, or up to the number of groups the value is written in, max 6), never a substring. Values of 1-2 characters match only a standalone word, and only in images; text scans skip them.",
    "fn normalize / tokens / alnum: expect is the output. fn tokenSim: expect.sim within 0.0001. fn clampThreshold: input -> expect (null stands for any non-number).",
    "fn termsOf: `vault` items -> expect, the list of [vaultId, text, digit] terms in order. Pins with an empty or generic label (GENERIC_PIN_LABELS) contribute no terms, aliases included (D-36, AC-088). Every other empty or generic string (normalised, in GENERIC_PIN_LABELS), label or alias, of any kind, contributes no term on its own (D-79).",
    "fn coords: coordinatesNearPins(text, pins, 1000 m): decimal numbers with >= 3 decimals, adjacent pairs tried as (lat, lng) and (lng, lat); expect is the pin's vaultId or null.",
    "All values are synthetic: no real people, homes, schools or plates (CLAUDE.md invariant 9). The pins are in the open Atlantic.",
    "Also (D-77): (1) the unjoined token sequence is scanned as well as the joined one, so a 1-2 letter label next to other single letters is not lost; (2) a single-token label of < 4 characters that is generic (or the fold of a generic word: st, rd, ave, no) never matches; (3) each word is also tried with a possessive 's removed (\"AVA'S\" -> \"AVA\"), so short names are caught; (4) Unicode format characters (soft hyphen, zero-width space) are deleted, not turned into a space; (5) digit kinds are matched on whole words AND on the sub-words punctuation separates (\"Tel:07700900123\", \"REG:SE1234\"), and the number of groups is counted on the normalised value; (6) each word is also read with format characters turned into spaces (a zero-width space may separate two words), and every reading counts; (7) the sub-word view of a digit value may join up to 6 sub-words (exact equality, never a substring)."
  ],
